 "uncertain": {
  "342fe4c267bab82f": "Hapax (Job 6:17); the sense of zarab is debated ('flow', 'burn', 'wax warm', 'shrink').",
  "1de0ec8b094ba976": "Hapax (Ps 72:6); zarzif is uncertain: dripping, shower or soaking rain.",
  "23b8454a707683cf": "Hapax (Prov 30:31); the animal 'girded of loins' is debated: rooster, greyhound, war horse, starling.",
  "775381d63e8bbdb7": "zaram is rare (2x); in Ps 90:5 'you flood them / sweep them away' is debated.",
  "c2af98b1cf8a3b29": "Hos 7:9: zaraq usually 'sprinkle'; 'gray hair has sneaked in / is sprinkled on him' is debated.",
  "9ad2003825a9a64d": "Job 38:30: hithpael of chaba 'hide' glossed 'become hard'; the waters 'hide themselves' or 'harden' is debated.",
  "5e23807a440c5152": "Prov 13:13: chabal here is read 'be pledged / held in pledge (bound to pay)' or 'be destroyed'; the sense is debated.",
  "4676051741e56b22": "Josh 19:29: mechebel read as 'from [the] region' or as the place name Mahalab; identification debated.",
  "4133f0e6c8c999fb": "Hapax (Prov 23:34): chibbel 'mast' or 'rigging'; the exact sense is debated.",
  "77ffba45a9af8e50": "chavatselet (Song 2:1): the flower is debated (crocus, rose, asphodel, narcissus).",
  "b4b8674eb35af538": "chavatselet (Isa 35:1): the flower is debated (crocus, rose, asphodel, narcissus).",
  "f7b56d70c6e53c68": "Job 34:17: chavash 'bind' glossed 'govern' (restrain, rule); the sense is debated.",
  "b7720db14072f38d": "2Sam 22:46: chagar here is read 'gird themselves' or 'come trembling / limp out'; the sense is debated.",
  "46f435fdad1f4d1f": "Isa 38:11: chedel 'cessation' is often read as cheled 'world'; the sense is debated.",
  "7f81828622dd7d32": "Hapax (Ezek 21:14): chadar 'surround' or 'enter into chambers'; the sense is debated.",
  "a528873e9c4f239a": "Job 41:30: chaddud (rare) 'sharp points of potsherds' describing the creature's underside; the image is debated."
 },
